  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4a2b061e491659d4e8424ca22aacc1c7, type: 3}
  m_Name: Read_ZoneProfile_Resources_Starter
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Hecton8.World.WorldExpeditionLoopProfile
  profileId: loop.profile.resources.starter
  profileLabel: Resources Starter Read
  entryBeat: A readable shelf, arch, or scrap silhouette makes the water easy to
    read at first glance.
  routineBeat: Common materials are visible quickly without forcing one exact sweep.
  reliefBeat: Short reorientation pockets let the player reassess and decide whether
    to keep wandering.
  pressureBeat: Risk rises naturally as visibility drops and easy materials thin
    out.
  payoffBeat: A stronger node or denser material patch exists deeper in for players
    who feel like pushing.
  exitBeat: Leaving stays readable by memory of shape and light, not by a prescribed
    line.
  playerFreedomRule: The player can drift, circle, detour, or leave at any time;
    this water only suggests confidence, not obedience.
  softProgressionPull: The place gently teaches that stronger finds usually sit a
    little beyond the most obvious shelf.
  optionalDetourRule: Side pockets should still teach the terrain and pay out a little
    value.
  returnLogic: Returning later should feel faster because the player remembers the
    shapes and material rhythm.
  masteryLogic: Mastery means building a personal quick-harvest loop, not following
    a designer path.
  playerPromise: Readable early water with recoverable value, mild risk, and room
    to improvise.
  routeMemoryRule: Memory should come from one strong silhouette and one reliable
    reorientation pocket.
  failureMode: If shapes, pressure, and value blur together, the area turns into
    mush.
